SUMMARY:❄️ Winter Solstice
DESCRIPTION:The day with the fewest daylight hours of the year in the Northern Hemisphere.\n\nEstimated daylight: 9h 44m (at 34.05°N)\nExact moment: 12:51 PM PST
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_solstice
CATEGORIES:Astronomy,Solar Events
COLOR:steelblue
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Winter Solstice
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
